sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Trader
    participant CD as CyberDeltaEngine
    participant RM as Risk Management
    participant BP as Backpack API (CEX)
    participant HL as Hyperliquid (Arbitrum)
    participant PX as Paradex (StarkNet)
    participant Bridge as L1/L2 Bridge (e.g., Across, Hop, Native)
    participant Wallet as L1/L2 Wallet

    Note over CD,Wallet: Enhanced Collateral Transfer Process (Critique-Informed Flow)

    %% Initialization with Pre-Positioning and Caching
    Note over RM: Initialization and Collateral Check Phase
    RM->>RM: Predict C_target^BP, C_target^HL, C_target^PX using ML (E[C_needed] + k * σ_C)
    RM->>BP: Get balance (ED25519-signed, check cache t_now - t_cache < 5min)
    BP-->>RM: C_current^BP (or cached value)
    RM->>HL: Get balance (REST, check cache t_now - t_cache < 5min)
    HL-->>RM: C_current^HL (or cached value)
    RM->>PX: Get balance (REST, check cache t_now - t_cache < 5min)
    PX-->>RM: C_current^PX (or cached value)
    RM->>RM: Check imbalance: If |C_current - C_target| < Tolerance (e.g., 0.02 * C_target), skip transfer.

    %% Transfer Decision Phase with Dynamic Pathing
    alt Significant Imbalance: |C_current^X - C_target^X| > Tolerance
        Note over RM: Transfer Decision Phase
        RM->>RM: Calculate transfer size: ΔC = C_target - C_current
        RM->>RM: Evaluate Paths (Direct, Bridge) using Cost = α*Fees + β*Time + γ*Risk
        RM->>RM: Factor in Urgency = w_urgency * t_deadline
        RM->>RM: Select Optimal Path (e.g., Path_Best)

        %% Option 1: Direct CEX → L2 Transfer (Enhanced with Batching & Contingency)
        opt Path_Best == Direct (e.g., BP → HL)
            Note over RM,HL: Direct Path: BP → HL
            RM->>RM: Determine chunks if ΔC > $50k: n_chunks = ΔC / $50k
            RM->>RM: Generate ED25519 signatures for each chunk withdrawal
            RM->>BP: Batch withdrawal requests (parallel, signed, to L2 address)
            Note right of BP: Handles security reviews for large amounts internally
            BP-->>RM: Multiple tx_ids (or single if small)
            loop Monitor Each Withdrawal (1-5min)
                RM->>BP: Check status (signed request)
                BP-->>RM: Status: pending → initiated → sent_to_bridge
            end
            Note right of BP: BP interacts with the appropriate L1/L2 bridge
            BP->>Bridge: Submit batched txs to Arbitrum bridge
            loop Monitor Bridge Deposit (e.g., Arbitrum 3-5min, StarkNet 10-30min)
                RM->>Bridge: Check bridge deposit status (via API or chain query)
                Bridge-->>RM: Status: pending → confirmed
                alt Bridge Delay > 10min
                    RM->>HL: Borrow ΔC temporarily (on-exchange)
                    HL-->>RM: Borrowing confirmed (or failed)
                    RM->>RM: Log temporary borrowing
                end
            end
            Bridge->>Wallet: Funds bridged to L2
            RM->>HL: Deposit funds from Wallet to HL exchange
            HL-->>RM: Deposit confirmed
            alt Borrowing was initiated
                RM->>HL: Repay borrowed ΔC
                HL-->>RM: Repayment confirmed
            end
            RM->>RM: Update C_current^BP -= ΔC, C_current^HL += ΔC
            RM->>CD: Notify: Transfer BP→HL complete
            CD->>User: Dashboard Update: "BP→HL: $ΔC transferred, ETA met/updated"

        %% Option 2: Bridge-Mediated Transfer (BP → L1 → Bridge → L2 or L2 → Bridge → L2)
        opt Path_Best == Bridge (e.g., BP → PX via Across)
            Note over RM,PX: Bridge Path Example: BP → PX via Across
            %% Step 1: Withdraw from Source (if CEX)
            alt Source == BP
                RM->>BP: Withdraw ΔC to L1 Wallet (signed request)
                BP-->>RM: tx_id
                loop Monitor Withdrawal (5-30min)
                    RM->>BP: Check status (signed)
                    BP-->>RM: Status update
                end
                BP->>Wallet: Funds on L1
            else Source == HL or PX
                 RM->>HL: Withdraw ΔC to L2 Wallet (e.g., Arbitrum Wallet)
                 HL-->>Wallet: Funds in L2 Wallet
            end

            %% Step 2: Bridge Selection & Execution
            RM->>RM: Check Liquidity: L_available(Across) vs ΔC? L_available(Hop) vs ΔC?
            RM->>RM: Select Best Bridge (e.g., Across based on cost/speed/liquidity)
            RM->>Bridge: Initiate Bridge Transfer (e.g., Across API Call/Contract Interaction)
            Note right of Bridge: Payload specifies source/dest chain, amount, recipient, fees
            Wallet->>Bridge: Sign & Send Transaction (Deposit to Spoke Pool if Across)
            Bridge-->>RM: Bridge transfer initiated (e.g., relayer searching)

            loop Check Bridge/Destination Status (Across: few mins, Native: longer)
                RM->>Bridge: Query bridge transfer status
                Bridge-->>RM: Status: Relaying / Bridging / Confirmed
            end
            Bridge->>Wallet: Funds arrive in Destination Wallet (e.g., StarkNet Wallet)

            %% Step 3: Deposit to Destination Exchange
            RM->>PX: Deposit funds from Wallet to PX exchange
            PX-->>RM: Deposit confirmed
            RM->>RM: Update C_current based on source/destination
            RM->>CD: Notify: Transfer complete via Bridge
            CD->>User: Dashboard Update: "Transfer Complete via Across, ETA met/updated"

        %% Option 3: L2-to-L2 Transfer (Simplified via direct L2 Bridge)
        opt Path_Best == L2_Bridge (e.g., HL → PX via Hop/Orbiter)
            Note over HL, PX: L2-to-L2 Path via specialized bridge (e.g., Hop)
            RM->>HL: Withdraw ΔC to Wallet (Arbitrum)
            HL-->>Wallet: Funds in Arbitrum Wallet

            RM->>Bridge: Initiate L2-L2 bridge transfer (e.g., Hop API/Contract)
            Wallet->>Bridge: Sign & Send Tx (Deposit to Hop)
            Bridge-->>RM: Bridge transfer initiated

            loop Check Bridge Status (e.g., Hop ~5-15min)
                 RM->>Bridge: Query bridge transfer status
                 Bridge-->>RM: Status: Bridging / Confirmed
            end
            Bridge->>Wallet: Funds arrive in StarkNet Wallet

            RM->>PX: Deposit funds from Wallet to PX exchange
            PX-->>RM: Deposit confirmed
            RM->>RM: Update C_current^HL -= ΔC, C_current^PX += ΔC
            RM->>CD: Notify: Transfer HL→PX complete via L2 Bridge
            CD->>User: Dashboard Update: "HL→PX: $ΔC transferred, ETA met/updated"
        end

        %% Interim Position Adjustment during transfer
        Note over RM, CD: Adjusting positions during transfer delay
        RM->>RM: Calculate Interim Scale Factor = C_current / C_target
        RM->>CD: Scale active positions: w_t = w_target * InterimScaleFactor

    end

    %% Error Handling with Automation & Path Switching
    alt Transfer Failure or Timeout
        Note over RM: Automated Error Handling Phase
        RM->>RM: Log failure: "Transfer Path_Best failed, tx_id: xyz, attempt: n"
        alt Retry Attempts < Max (e.g., 3)
            RM->>RM: Increment retry count n
            RM->>RM: Reduce size: Retry_Size = ΔC / 2^n
            RM->>RM: Evaluate alternative paths (e.g., Bridge if Direct failed)
            RM->>RM: Select New_Path_Best
            Note right of RM: Trigger transfer using New_Path_Best with Retry_Size
            RM->>RM: Initiate new transfer (similar to above flows)
        else Max Retries Reached
            RM->>CD: Alert: "Transfer failed after max retries. Manual intervention needed."
            CD->>User: Dashboard Alert: "TRANSFER FAILED - REQUIRES ACTION"
            %% Trigger Full Reconciliation
            RM->>RM: Initiate balance reconciliation across all exchanges
            RM->>BP: Get balance (signed)
            BP-->>RM: C_actual^BP
            RM->>HL: Get balance
            HL-->>RM: C_actual^HL
            RM->>PX: Get balance
            PX-->>RM: C_actual^PX
            RM->>RM: Update C_current = C_actual, Log discrepancy: |C_expected - C_actual|
        end
    end

    %% Post-Transfer Adjustment (Final)
    Note over CD,RM: Post-Transfer Final Adjustment Phase
    RM->>RM: Final reconciliation check (if not done in error handling)
    RM->>RM: Update C_available = ∑ C_current^i
    RM->>RM: Update Kelly sizing: f* = (π - Costs) / σ^2
    RM-->>CD: Updated final parameters
    CD->>CD: Unscale positions / Adjust to final target size 